  "en": {
    "title": "Tree Dream Meaning — Korean Dream Interpretation (나무 꿈해몽)",
    "metaDescription": "What does dreaming of a tree mean in Korean tradition? Lush trees, falling trees, planting dreams, dead trees blooming — complete auspicious and ominous interpretations explained.",
    "h1": "Tree Dream Meaning in Korean Interpretation — What the Tree's Condition Reveals",
    "intro": "If a lush, magnificent tree appeared in your dream last night, Korean dream tradition reads it as clear evidence that positive energy is flooding into your life right now. In Korean 해몽 (dream interpretation), trees are far more than plants — they are sacred cosmic pillars connecting heaven and earth, and the traditional dwelling place of village guardian spirits. A tree in full bloom or laden with fruit is one of the finest auspicious signs imaginable. But here's the thing: even a dead tree holds a dramatic plot twist in Korean interpretation, one that can flip an ominous dream into an extraordinary good omen.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Auspicious: Lush and Thriving Tree Dreams",
        "content": "In Korean dream interpretation (해몽), a healthy tree full of lush green leaves is one of the clearest signals of incoming prosperity. This dream suggests that positive energy is flowing freely through your career, household, and finances. A large tree growing inside the home or being moved indoors is especially auspicious — it implies that wealth will enter the household, or that you will become a key figure in your organization and attract talented people to your side.\n\nA tree covered in blossoms or heavy with fruit is considered among the finest auspicious dreams in the entire 해몽 tradition. It signals that financial fortune and career advancement are aligned in your favor. Picking fruit directly from the tree additionally carries pregnancy symbolism (태몽) — it may foretell the birth of a gifted child."
      },
      {
        "heading": "The Miraculous Reversal: Dead Tree Sprouting New Life",
        "content": "One of the most dramatic and celebrated dream patterns in Korean tradition is the dead tree that suddenly comes back to life — sprouting new buds or bursting into unexpected bloom. This is called 기사회생 (rising from death), and it is a deeply auspicious sign. Projects you had given up on will resume; unexpected windfalls will arrive; long-stalled situations will break open overnight. For those who have been ill, this dream may signal recovery. No matter how bleak things appear, this dream says: the universe still has a turnaround waiting for you.",
        "imageRef": "auspicious"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Inauspicious: Falling or Uprooted Tree Dreams",
        "content": "A tree knocked down by wind, struck by lightning, or uprooted from the ground is an inauspicious sign in Korean dream tradition. The most common interpretation is that a key person you have relied upon — a mentor, a parent, a business partner — is about to depart or retire. In business terms, it warns that an important foundation or contract may collapse. For the household, it may signal health concerns for the head of the family.\n\nThe more violent the fall — especially if caused by lightning — the more sudden and unexpected the warning. After dreaming of a falling tree, it is wise to check in on health, review the stability of ongoing commitments, and avoid rushing into major decisions.",
        "imageRef": "inauspicious"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Inauspicious: Dead, Withered, or Bare-Branched Tree",
        "content": "A tree that is dead, dried out, or completely stripped of leaves carries a warning about depleted life force. This dream is typically interpreted as a signal of declining health, financial difficulty, or business stagnation. For those already unwell, it serves as an especially strong prompt to prioritize rest and medical attention.\n\nCrucially, however, the meaning flips entirely if the dead tree sprouts new growth during the same dream. Always pay close attention to how the dream ends — the final image is the key to the correct interpretation."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Inauspicious: Cutting or Chopping Down a Tree",
        "content": "Dreaming of chopping down, axing, or sawing through a tree is a classic warning of financial loss in Korean tradition. Because trees symbolize the household's life force and wealth, destroying one in a dream represents cutting off your own prosperity. Cutting trees in the yard specifically warns of theft or monetary setbacks. Cutting a tree inside the home additionally suggests health concerns for a family member. The larger the tree being cut, the greater the implied financial impact — take this dream as a prompt to review spending and postpone risky financial decisions."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Neutral: Climbing a Tree Dream",
        "content": "Tree-climbing dreams are all about the outcome. If you reach the top of the tree safely and easily, it is an auspicious dream predicting promotion, goal achievement, or exam success — a smooth rise to a higher position. If you slip or fall from the tree, however, it warns of instability in your current position or a setback in an ongoing project. Rather than discouraging, this dream is more of a practical caution: reassess what might be making your current climb precarious, and reinforce your foundations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Tree Dreams and Seasonal Context",
        "content": "Season matters in Korean tree dream interpretation. A spring tree with fresh new leaves or flowers signals new beginnings — a new venture, a new relationship, a fresh start. A summer tree in full green suggests current projects are thriving and growing strong. An autumn tree dressed in fall colors points to harvest time, completion, and taking stock of what you have built. A bare winter tree is not necessarily ominous — it represents a period of quiet reflection and inner preparation, with spring inevitably waiting on the other side."
      }
    ],
